{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001625-uk-london-callin-in-wod","id":1001625,"title":"UK/London Callin in WoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-10T21:42:22-08:00","id":1001625,"title":"UK/London Callin in WoD?","content":"i love the UK, never been there though.<br /> <br /> i was wondering if theres any settingbook for the UK, i been wanting to ST a Mage campaing in that place and i cant seem to find much info","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:28:44-08:00","id":1001657,"title":"","content":"Victorian Age: Vampire<br /> Bloody Hearts: Diablerie Britain (Only just learned this one even existed, can't vouch for it.)<br /> London by Night (Victorian Age)<br /> A World of Darkness (1st and 2nd edition)<br /> Dark Ages: British Isles (Pretty weak and inaccurate)<br /> <br /> These are the main books. Speaking as someone born and raised in England I was always disappointed with the lack of attention (seriously, modern London by night should have been a no-brainer) but that just inspired me to build my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 11-11-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:30:35-08:00","id":1001672,"title":"","content":"For Vampire; Basicly the British Isles has been ruled by a Ventrue Methuselah named Mithras since the romans started invading the islands. He has had several seneschals and chamberlains during this time, among them the Cappadocian Lord Camden and the Ventrue Lady Anne Bowsley. Lady Anne took over as Prince after the bombings of London during WW2 when Mithras was thought destroyed, naming herself Queen Anne of London.<br /> In the events between 2nd Edition and Revised edition Mithras woke up from torpor, fought a pack of werewolves, and in his weakened state after the fight he was found and diablerized by an Assamite Antitribu named Monty Coven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T04:51:07-08:00","id":1001714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001625-uk-london-callin-in-wod?p=1001657#post1001657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorian Age: Vampire<br /> Bloody Hearts: Diablerie Britain (Only just learned this one even existed, can't vouch for it.)<br /> London by Night (Victorian Age)<br /> A World of Darkness (1st and 2nd edition)<br /> Dark Ages: British Isles (Pretty weak and inaccurate)<br /> <br /> These are the main books. Speaking as someone born and raised in England I was always disappointed with the lack of attention (seriously, modern London by night should have been a no-brainer) but that just inspired me to build my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling's Isle of the Mighty, too, which isn't held in high regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:48:49-08:00","id":1001864,"title":"","content":"For WoD, and considering that you actualy like the UK, I strongly recommend that you look in for some pieces of information from the cannon, like Mithras' history, and them just fill the gaps yourself. You surely knows more about UK than WW staff ever knew.<br /> <br /> You know more about any freaking country outside the USA than any WW staff ever knew.<br /> <br /> By the way, @Elizabeth Sterling, if you found their portrait of London (and Great Britain at large) disappointing, you should see what they did to Brazil, or any other &quot;third world&quot; country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:28:51-08:00","id":1002574,"title":"","content":"Ha! Twenty years later I recall being flabbergasted that the Montreal citybook featured ultra-violent cainites turning to American football as their leisure activity of choice, with nary a mention of the popularity of hockey in the present day or its role in past political history. And some of the writers were Canadian!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}